```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Operators running memory-constrained agentic LLM serving with many distinct system+tool-schema prefix families (K≥8), heavy load (queue depth >1), and small batch slots (B≈4), where GPU KV cache cannot hold all families simultaneously.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only at L0; conditional 5–10% mean prefill-token savings (up to 76% in narrow cell) at matched p99, but zero win when cache holds all families or load is light. No wall-clock, no real vLLM/SGLang, no paged-attention allocator, no TTFT measurement. Advantage likely erodes in production where (a) caches are provisioned to hold hot prefixes, (b) larger batches dilute reordering leverage, and (c) existing cache-aware schedulers (SGLang RadixAttention, vLLM APC) already capture the greedy benefit.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Requires scheduler modification in vLLM/SGLang to track family residency and enforce bounded reorder window; tuning W per deployment to hold p99 ≤1.10× FCFS; risk of p99 regression if W mis-set; complexity vs. existing cache-aware admission; lack of real-GPU validation; benefit vanishes if operator simply sizes cache to cover working set (the honest-negative N2 regime).]
RATIONALE: EXP-0005 shows PARTIAL conditional HELD: 15/92 matched-fairness cells win (CI<0), all in {one,few}×heavy, mean 5.8% (one) and 5.0% (few) prefill savings at p99 ratio ~1.02, zero wins (0/32) when cache holds all K (N2 fires) [packet]. Strongest wins at B=4, K=8/16, heavy load, up to 76% token reduction, but light load yields ~0.3% [packet]. Unbounded greedy gains 17% mean but at 1.29–1.34× p99 blowup, confirming fairness cost [packet]. L0 uses constant-time service and token-count proxy, not wall-clock TTFT/throughput, no real paged kernel, no vLLM/SGLang scheduler, no APC/RadixAttention [packet]. Prior-art caveat notes SGLang cache-aware/RadixAttention and vLLM scheduler+APC are known; novelty is narrowly the matched-fairness bounded-W control, not cache-aware admission itself [packet]. Operationally, provisioning KV cache to hold hot prefix families (the N2 regime) is standard practice and eliminates the win; small-B heavy-load regime may not match production where batches are larger and caches are sized for working set. Actionable guidance from negative result: size cache ≥ working-set families or accept that PFA offers no benefit under light load or ample cache.
```
